===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-|id=shiny}}
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:enflaumen|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|inflammen}}, {{m|enm|enflamen}}, {{m|enm|enflaumen|t=to set (something) on fire; to be on fire; (''figurative'') to enrage (someone); to become enraged; to incite (someone) to do evil; to inspire (someone); (''medicine'') to cause inflammation of (a body part)}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=enflaumen|pos=v|id=MED13775}}</ref> from {{der|en|fro|enflamer}}, {{m|fro|enflammer|t=to set (something) on fire, inflame; to be on fire; (''figurative'') to fuel (a debate, hatred, etc.)}} (modern {{cog|fr|enflammer}}), from {{der|en|la|inflammāre}}, the {{lg|present}} {{lg|active}} {{lg|infinitive}} of {{m|la|inflammō|t=to set (something) on fire, inflame; (''figurative'') to excite (someone)}}, from {{m|la|in-|pos={{lg|prefix}} meaning ‘into; to, towards’}} + {{m|la|flammō|t=to set (something) on fire; to be on fire; (''figurative'') to incite (someone)}}<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=1797530247|date=March 2026|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref> (from {{m|la|flamma|t=flame, fire; (''figurative'') passion}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-|*bʰel-, *bʰl̥g-|to blaze, burn; to glow, shine; bright flame, fire}}) + {{m|la|-ō|pos=suffix forming regular first-{{lg|conjugation}} {{lg|verb}}s}}). {{surf|en|in-|pos1=prefix meaning ‘into; to, towards’|flame}}.

