##* {{RQ:T. Herbert Travaile|edition=4th|chapter=[Law Rigidly Executed]|page=211|passage=[F]orty Camels entring loaden vvith Tobacco out of ''India'', (the drivers being ignorant of a late prohibition, the King ſometimes commanding and reſtraining as reaſon of State invited,) ''Mamet Ally-beg'' {{...}} offering vvithal to his angry Juſtice a diſmal ſacrifice of forty load of Tobacco vvhich vvas put into a deep hole that ſerved as a pipe, and being '''inflamed''', in a black vapour gave the Citizens ''gratis'' for tvvo vvhole days and nights an unpleaing incenſe.}}
